WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:05.030
MeetRec records your meetings, and knows who said what.

2
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.126
When a Google Meet, Teams, or Slack huddle starts,

3
00:00:09.176 --> 00:00:12.374
it offers to record, right from the menu bar.

4
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.951
Afterwards, every line of the transcript is labeled with its speaker:

5
00:00:17.001 --> 00:00:19.409
you, and everyone else on the call.

6
00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.735
See how long each person talked, at a glance.

7
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.061
Click a person to see every turn they spoke.

8
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.086
Pick one, and playback jumps right to that moment.

9
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.950
Then, ask the AI you already use.

10
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.127
MeetRec talks to Claude Code or Codex, right on your Mac.

11
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:50.125
It uses your own login, so there's no extra API key.

12
00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.903
You can also import a recording,

13
00:00:54.953 --> 00:00:58.732
or paste a YouTube, podcast, or Spotify link.

14
00:00:58.796 --> 00:01:02.563
It's transcribed the same way, speaker by speaker.

15
00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:05.948
Transcription runs on your Mac by default,

16
00:01:05.998 --> 00:01:09.986
or in the cloud, with your own Groq or OpenAI key.

17
00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:16.310
It's free and open source, for macOS 15 and later on Apple Silicon.

18
00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:19.546
Get it at meetrec.dorara.app.
